    "details": "# Problem Description:\n\nThe ELF core dump code counted the number of dumpable VM map entries,\nallocated a buffer for the corresponding program headers, then iterated\nover the map a second time to populate them. A process sharing the\naddress space via rfork(2) can mutate the map between the two passes,\ncausing the second pass to write program headers past the end of the\nbuffer.\n\n# Impact:\n\nAn unprivileged local user sharing an address space with a process that\ndumps core can trigger an out-of-bounds write on the kernel heap,\npotentially leading to privilege escalation.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0370",
